{"name":"Blue-Eyed Cryptid","hex":"#5c767f","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"eyed","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having eyes.","Having eye-like spots."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of eye"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eyed"},{"term":"cryptid","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A creature known only from folklore or legend, the existence of which is not proven by scientific observation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cryptid"}],"entries":[{"title":"List of cryptids","blocks":[{"text":"Cryptids are animals or other beings whose present existence is disputed or unsubstantiated by science. Cryptozoology, the study of cryptids, is a pseudoscience claiming that such beings may exist somewhere in the wild; it has been widely critiqued by scientists. The subculture is regularly criticized for reliance on anecdotal information and because in the course of investigating animals that most scientists believe are unlikely to have existed, cryptozoologists do not follow the scientific method. Many scientists have criticized the plausibility of cryptids due to lack of physical evidence, likely misidentifications and misinterpretation of stories from folklore. While biologists regularly identify new species following established scientific methodology, cryptozoologists focus on entities mentioned in the folklore record and rumor."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_cryptids","wikidata":"Q16322"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Bunyip_1890.jpg/500px-Bunyip_1890.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Bunyip_1890.jpg/500px-Bunyip_1890.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABunyip_1890.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Cadborosaurus_October_1937.jpg/500px-Cadborosaurus_October_1937.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Cadborosaurus_October_1937.jpg/1280px-Cadborosaurus_October_1937.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Cadborosaurus_October_1937.jpg/500px-Cadborosaurus_October_1937.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACadborosaurus_October_1937.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Artistic_representation_of_Sandra_Mansi%27s_1977_photograph_of_%22Champ%22_lake_monster.jpg/500px-Artistic_representation_of_Sandra_Mansi%27s_1977_photograph_of_%22Champ%22_lake_monster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Artistic_representation_of_Sandra_Mansi%27s_1977_photograph_of_%22Champ%22_lake_monster.jpg/1280px-Artistic_representation_of_Sandra_Mansi%27s_1977_photograph_of_%22Champ%22_lake_monster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Artistic_representation_of_Sandra_Mansi%27s_1977_photograph_of_%22Champ%22_lake_monster.jpg/500px-Artistic_representation_of_Sandra_Mansi%